## 3. `ss.c` – replicated writes and sync handlers

### 3.1. Accept replicated writes

Add a helper to apply a write directly to main storage (not temp sessions) when acting as replica. We can reuse `write_file_ss()` but pass a special username and treat it as a normal write on the main file.

Simpler: add a new function `replicated_write_file_ss()` that writes to the **primary file** and updates content exactly like `write_file_ss`, but without sessions. To keep scope small, we’ll just open the main file, parse,

, and write back.

Add near other file ops:

```c
````c
// filepath: /home/shrawani/course-project-shellshocked/ss.c
// ...existing prototypes...
int write_file_ss(const char *filename, const char* username, int sent_idx, int word_idx, const char *content);
int stream_file_ss(int client_sock, const char *filename);
int get_file_info_ss(const char *filename, FileMetadata *meta);
// ...existing prototypes...

// NEW: apply replicated write directly to main file (used when this SS is a replica)
static int replicated_write_file_ss(const char *filename,
                                    int sent_idx,
                                    int word_idx,
                                    const char *content) {
    char filepath[MAX_PATH];
    snprintf(filepath, sizeof(filepath), "%s/%s", ss.storage_path, filename);

    FileContent *fc = init_file_content();
    if (parse_file(filepath, fc) != 0) {
        // treat as empty file
        fc->sentence_count = 1;
        fc->sentences[0].capacity = SENTENCE_CAPACITY;
        fc->sentences[0].word_count = 0;
        fc->sentences[0].words = malloc(sizeof(char*) * fc->sentences[0].capacity);
    }

    if (fc->sentence_count == 0) {
        fc->sentence_count = 1;
        fc->sentences[0].capacity = SENTENCE_CAPACITY;
        fc->sentences[0].word_count = 0;
        fc->sentences[0].words = malloc(sizeof(char*) * fc->sentences[0].capacity);
    }

    if (sent_idx < 0 || sent_idx > fc->sentence_count) {
        log_formatted(LOG_ERROR, "[REPL] Invalid sentence index %d for %s", sent_idx, filename);
        free_file_content(fc);
        return ERR_INVALID_INDEX;
    }

    int rc = insert_word_in_sentence(fc, sent_idx, word_idx, content);
    if (rc < 0) {
        free_file_content(fc);
        return ERR_INVALID_INDEX;
    }

    if (write_file_content(filepath, fc) != 0) {
        log_formatted(LOG_ERROR, "[REPL] Failed to write replicated content to %s", filepath);
        free_file_content(fc);
        return ERR_SERVER_ERROR;
    }

    free_file_content(fc);
    log_formatted(LOG_INFO, "[REPL] Applied replicated write to %s (sent=%d, word=%d)",
                  filename, sent_idx, word_idx);
    return SUCCESS;
}
