The disappearance of `printf("locked the mutex\n");` is not because the mutex “can’t be locked”; it’s because you’re **deadlocking on the same mutex twice** in the same thread.

From your current code:

````c
```c
// filepath: /home/shrawani/course-project-shellshocked/nm.c

// 1) In handle_ss_connection:
void* handle_ss_connection(void* arg) {
    ...
    pthread_mutex_lock(&nm.ss_mutex);
    ...
