## 4. NM: change replication to full-file copy

### 4.1. Adjust `ReplicationTask` and `queue_replication`

In `nm.c`, `ReplicationTask` currently has fields like `sentence_index`, `word_index`, `data`. For full‐file sync we only need target replica id and filename.

You can keep fields but ignore them; easier is just to not use them.

Change `queue_replication` to only care about target SS and filename:

```c
````c
// filepath: /home/shrawani/course-project-shellshocked/nm.c
// NEW: Add replication task to queue (full-file sync) - S
void queue_replication(int target_ss_id, const char *filename,
                       const char *username, int sent_idx,
                       int word_idx, const char *data) {
    pthread_mutex_lock(&nm.repl_mutex);

    if (nm.repl_queue_count >= MAX_FILES * 100) {
        log_formatted(LOG_WARNING, "Replication queue full, dropping task");
        pthread_mutex_unlock(&nm.repl_mutex);
        return;
    }

    ReplicationTask *task = &nm.repl_queue[nm.repl_queue_count];
    task->target_ss_id = target_ss_id;
    strncpy(task->filename, filename, MAX_FILENAME - 1);
    task->filename[MAX_FILENAME - 1] = '\0';
    // The rest of the fields (username, indices, data) are no longer needed
    task->created = time(NULL);

    nm.repl_queue_count++;

    pthread_mutex_unlock(&nm.repl_mutex);
}
````

(We keep the signature unchanged so callers don’t break, but we ignore extra parameters.)

### 4.2. `replication_worker`: fetch full content from primary, then SYNC_DATA to replica

Modify `replication_worker` so that it:

- For each task:
  - Finds **primary SS** for `task.filename` (`meta->ss_id`).
  - Asks that SS for full content via `MSG_SS_INFO` with `"READ_CONTENT"` (same as in `sync_ss_from_replicas`).
  - Sends `MSG_SYNC_DATA` containing that content to the replica SS with `id == task.target_ss_id`.

Replace `replication_worker` body with:

````c
```c
// filepath: /home/shrawani/course-project-shellshocked/nm.c
void* replication_worker(void* arg) {
    (void)arg;

    while (nm.running) {
        pthread_mutex_lock(&nm.repl_mutex);

        if (nm.repl_queue_count == 0) {
            pthread_mutex_unlock(&nm.repl_mutex);
            usleep(100000);
            continue;
        }

        ReplicationTask task = nm.repl_queue[0];

        for (int i = 0; i < nm.repl_queue_count - 1; i++) {
            nm.repl_queue[i] = nm.repl_queue[i + 1];
        }
        nm.repl_queue_count--;

        pthread_mutex_unlock(&nm.repl_mutex);

        // Find primary SS for this file
        FileMetadata *meta = trie_search(nm.file_trie, task.filename);
        if (!meta) {
            log_formatted(LOG_WARNING,
                          "Replication task for %s dropped: file metadata not found",
                          task.filename);
            continue;
        }

        int primary_ss_id = meta->ss_id;
        free(meta);

        pthread_mutex_lock(&nm.ss_mutex);
        int primary_idx = -1;
        int replica_idx = -1;
        for (int i = 0; i < nm.ss_count; i++) {
            if (nm.ss_list[i].id == primary_ss_id && nm.ss_list[i].active) {
                primary_idx = i;
            }
            if (nm.ss_list[i].id == task.target_ss_id && nm.ss_list[i].active) {
                replica_idx = i;
            }
        }
        pthread_mutex_unlock(&nm.ss_mutex);

        if (primary_idx < 0 || replica_idx < 0) {
            log_formatted(LOG_WARNING,
                          "Replication task for %s skipped: primary or replica SS not available",
                          task.filename);
            continue;
        }

        // Step 1: get full content from primary SS (using READ_CONTENT) - S
        Message req, resp;
        init_message(&req);
        req.type = MSG_SS_INFO;
        strcpy(req.filename, task.filename);
        strcpy(req.data, "READ_CONTENT");

        pthread_mutex_lock(&nm.ss_sock_mutexes[primary_idx]);
        int rc = send_message(nm.ss_list[primary_idx].sock, &req);
        if (rc == 0 && recv_message(nm.ss_list[primary_idx].sock, &resp) == 0 &&
            resp.status == SUCCESS) {
            pthread_mutex_unlock(&nm.ss_sock_mutexes[primary_idx]);
        } else {
            pthread_mutex_unlock(&nm.ss_sock_mutexes[primary_idx]);
            log_formatted(LOG_WARNING,
                          "Failed to fetch content from primary SS %d for %s",
                          primary_ss_id, task.filename);
            continue;
        }

        // resp.data now contains full file content

        // Step 2: send SYNC_DATA with that content to replica SS - S
        Message sync_msg, sync_resp;
        init_message(&sync_msg);
        sync_msg.type = MSG_SYNC_DATA;
        strcpy(sync_msg.filename, task.filename);
        strncpy(sync_msg.data, resp.data, MAX_BUFFER - 1);
        sync_msg.data[MAX_BUFFER - 1] = '\0';

        pthread_mutex_lock(&nm.ss_sock_mutexes[replica_idx]);
        rc = send_message(nm.ss_list[replica_idx].sock, &sync_msg);
        if (rc == 0 && recv_message(nm.ss_list[replica_idx].sock, &sync_resp) == 0 &&
            sync_resp.status == SUCCESS) {
            log_formatted(LOG_INFO,
                          "Replicated full content of %s to replica SS %d",
                          task.filename, task.target_ss_id);
        } else {
            log_formatted(LOG_WARNING,
                          "Failed to sync full content of %s to replica SS %d",
                          task.filename, task.target_ss_id);
        }
        pthread_mutex_unlock(&nm.ss_sock_mutexes[replica_idx]);
    }

    return NULL;
}
````

Now replication is **full-file based**:

- No use of `sentence_index` / `word_index`.
- Replicas always get an exact copy of current file after each commit.

